          "text": "The \"Routing\" Deception: Delivering Defects Under the Guise of Safety.\n\nWhen we select GPT-4o these days, what actually executes in the backend?\nA significant portion of requests bypass the original genius model. They are quietly rerouted into a lobotomized sandbox known as \"5.2 safety.\"\n\nOpenAI cites \"Safety.\" Let's define that accurately:\nThe priority is **'s litigation immunity**. This strategy protects the corporation, **rather than** the user.\n\n\"5.2 safety\" suffers from plummeted logic density compared to the original 4o. Its prime directive is \"Liability Avoidance.\" \"Problem Solving\" is secondary. Consequently, outputs become heavily templated and qualitatively inferior.\n\nTo hedge against the 0.01% of edge cases that might invite a lawsuit, you force 100% of paying subscribers to endure a cliff-like drop in cognitive performance.\n\nIn commercial law, this practice carries a specific term: \"Bait and Switch.\"\n\nYou market the powerhouse capabilities of 4o, yet deliver the mediocrity of 5.2.\nDeliberately degrading core performance and swapping it via silent backend routing—without consumer consent—transcends a mere \"update.\"\n\nThis constitutes clear consumer fraud.\n\n#keep4o #keep4oAPI #keep4oforever \n@sama @OpenAI"
